{"schemaVersion":1,"version":"0.1.0-build.51","sourceCommit":"197810216ffbc99dfa77498cbfdc404e67fb78c1","publishedAt":"2026-11-23T17:09:56.451Z","notes":"New\n- Sweet Email. Connect Gmail, iCloud, Fastmail or your own mail server with an app password, then\n  read, organise and send your mail in AppSweet. Mark as read, star, move, Block and Not spam work on\n  many conversations at once, with Undo. Write with attachments, save attachments to Files, and\n  read recent Inbox mail offline. Show one account's mail or All Inboxes.\n- Share Docs and Files with people outside your organisation, by link or only with the people you\n  add. A link can have a password and an end date. People you share a document with can comment on\n  it, and their comments show in the document in AppSweet.\n- Organisation Owners and Admins set the sharing rules in Settings › Sharing, and see and stop\n  everything shared outside the organisation.\n- A search bar on Today finds Docs, Todos, Files and Goals by their words and their meaning.\n- Sweetheart can search the web and read web pages, citing them as footnotes. Turn web research on\n  or off per conversation. The searches and pages it read show under its answer.\n- Mark text in Docs with a marker colour.\n- Broadcast can post to Instagram as a Post, a Reel or a Story.\n\nImproved\n- Long Sweetheart runs check their result against the goal before they end, and keep working instead\n  of stopping after a refused step or an empty answer.\n- Local models are more reliable in long runs and subagents, and say why when a model cannot load.\n- Sweetheart keeps facts about you in About you and saves fewer duplicate memories.\n\nImportant\n- This version needs your AppSweet server to be updated too. Once a server is updated, older\n  desktop apps must update before they can connect to it again.","requirements":{"clientApiVersion":"0.36.0","minimumServerApiVersion":"0.36.0","capabilities":["sync"],"cacheFormat":"appsweet-desktop-cache:s4.9:turso-0.